University Tuition and Fee Policy

This sample policy document describes tuition payment responsibilities, fee deadlines, refunds, and student account holds. It is included as a public-style policy document for the local RAG lab corpus. Students are expected to review the tuition schedule before registration and confirm that all charges on the student account are accurate.

Tuition is billed by semester. Payment is due before the published deadline unless the student has an approved payment plan. A late payment fee may be applied when payment is not received by the deadline. The finance office may place a registration hold on accounts with unpaid balances.

Refunds are calculated according to the official withdrawal date. A full refund is available only before instruction begins. Partial refunds may be available during the first weeks of the semester. Administrative fees, technology fees, and service charges may be non-refundable depending on the category of charge.

Students receiving scholarships or financial aid remain responsible for any balance not covered by an award. If an award is revised, cancelled, or delayed, the student must pay the remaining balance by the adjusted due date. The university may request additional documentation to verify eligibility for tuition assistance.

International students must maintain valid payment records for visa and enrollment verification. Sponsored students should submit billing authorization documents before the start of the semester. Missing authorization may delay invoice processing and can result in a temporary account hold.

Appeals may be submitted to the finance office within thirty calendar days after the charge appears on the student account. Appeals must include the student ID, term, charge description, supporting documents, and a clear explanation of the requested adjustment.

